NOTE [written] A4.W1  -- the general construction (written, W-A4.2): for a closed K that contains the products, lies in maxCone and is a convex cone, its normalized slice S is compact (landed design lemma abs_le_one_of_maxCone bounds it, closedness of K closes it) and convex; take a countable dense Q in S; stage n has preparations q_1..q_n and the product labels of finitely many effects including the four basis effects; values lie in [0,1] because S lies in the normalized maxCone (as R1 checks on instances). The completion body is Psi(cl conv Q) = Psi(S) (Psi is an injective linear map out of a finite-dimensional space, hence a closed embedding), so the system has finite rank, its read-out image is S, and the cone over S is K.

